{title: Brain Damage}
{artist: Pink Floyd}
{key: D}

{c: Verse 1}
[D]The lunatic is on the [G7]grass,        [D]The lunatic is on the [G7]grass
[D]Remembering games and,        [E]daisy chains and laughs
[A7]Got to keep the loonies,        on the [D]path.
[D]The lunatic is in the [G7]hall,        [D]The lunatics are in my [G7]hall
[D]The paper holds their folded,        [E]faces to the floor
And [A7]every day the paperboy,        brings [D]more
[D/F#]And if the dam breaks open,        [E]many years too soon
[G]And if there is no room,        [D/F#]upon the hill
[D/F#]And if your head explodes,        with [E]dark forbodings too
Ill [G]see you on,        the dark side of the [D/F#]moon.
[D]The lunatic is in my [G7]head,        [D]The lunatic is in my [G7]head
[D]You raise the blade,        [E]you make the change
[A7]You rearrange me till Im [D]sane,        [D]You lock the door and
[E]throw away the key,        Theres [A7]someone in my head
but its not [D]me,        [D/F#]And if the cloud bursts
[E]thunder in your ear,        [G]You shout and
no one seems to [D/F#]hear,        [D/F#]And if the band youre in starts
[E]playing different tunes,        Ill [G]see you on
the dark side of the [D/F#]moon.        I cant think of anything to say except...
I think its marvellous! HaHaHa!"
